The current implementation is a naive split by newline and comma. I need to implement a proper CSV parser that handles:

1. Commas as field separators
2. LF and CRLF record endings (so handle \r\n)
3. Quoted fields containing commas/newlines
4. Escaped double quotes represented as two double quotes ("")
5. Empty fields
6. A final record without a newline
7. No trailing record separator should add an extra empty row
8. Empty input returns []
9. Reject unclosed quoted field with SyntaxError
10. Preserve spaces within fields

Let me write a proper CSV parser in JavaScript.

The algorithm:
- If text is empty, return []
- Split into records by newlines (handling \r\n)
- For each record, parse fields:
  - Track whether we're inside quotes
  - When not in quotes: split on commas
  - When in quotes: accumulate characters including commas and newlines
  - Handle escaped quotes ("")
  - Empty fields are allowed

Let me think about the parsing logic more carefully.

A standard CSV parser approach:
1. Iterate through characters
2. If we encounter a quote, enter quoted mode
3. If we encounter an unescaped quote inside a quoted field, it's an error (unclosed quote)
4. When not in quotes and we hit a comma, end the current field
5. When not in quotes and we hit a newline, end the record

Let me write this:

```javascript
export function parseCSV(text) {
  if (typeof text !== 'string') return [];
  if (text === '') return [];

  const records = [];
  let currentRecord = '';
  let inQuotes = false;
  let i = 0;

  while (i <= text.length) {
    const char = text[i];

    if (i === text.length) {
      // End of input
      if (currentRecord !== '') {
        records.push(currentRecord.split(',').map(f => f.trim()));
      }
      break;
    }

    if (char === '"') {
      // Check for escaped quote ""
      if (inQuotes && i + 1 < text.length && text[i + 1] === '"') {
        currentRecord += '"';
        i += 2;
        continue;
      } else {
        inQuotes = !inQuotes;
        if (inQuotes) {
          currentRecord += '"';
        } else {
          // End of quoted field
          currentRecord += '"';
        }
        i++;
        continue;
      }
    }

    if (char === '\n') {
      // End of record
      records.push(currentRecord.split(',').map(f => f.trim()));
      currentRecord = '';
      i++;
      continue;
    }

    if (char === ',' && !inQuotes) {
      records.push(currentRecord.split(',').map(f => f.trim()));
      currentRecord = '';
      i++;
      continue;
    }

    currentRecord += char;
    i++;
  }

  return records;
}
```

